# kills: the CSS breakpoint and desktopMQ agree at 1050x800 and 1023x800
# suite: node --test --test-name-pattern ^the.CSS.breakpoint.and.desktopMQ.agree.at.1050x800.and.1023x800$ tests/e2e.test.js
# Reviewer finding N1: the breakpoint is written twice - once in the CSS
# @media (min-width:1024px) rule, once in desktopMQ's own matchMedia()
# string. Drifting the JS side to 1100px (while the CSS stays at 1024px)
# means the CSS already presents the sidebar and hides the trigger at
# 1050x800, but desktopMQ.matches is still false there, so openPanel()/
# closePanel() keep treating the panel as the below-breakpoint modal -
# role="dialog" and an inert main are never shed even though the trigger
# that would let a user reach them has already gone display:none.
# Refreshed 2026-09-29 (lane S2): only the line number moved; panelStops()
# right below now inserts #modeS and a conditional seq-source-link entry,
# which does not touch the mutated desktopMQ line itself.
diff --git a/index.html b/index.html
--- a/index.html
+++ b/index.html
